%
% Backward goal: recursive ancestor with a STEP budget (max_steps=2).
% The full ancestor set of a over a→b→c→d is {b,c,d}. The native semi-naive
% governor stops after 2 committed derivations and returns a sound partial subset
% with status "exhausted" — budgeted backward queries now run on the native core.
:- prefix(ex, 'https://example.org/profiles/goal-budget-steps/').
ex:ancestor(X,Y) :- ex:parentOf(X,Y).
ex:ancestor(X,Y) :- ex:parentOf(X,Z), ex:ancestor(Z,Y).
?- ex:ancestor(ex:a, Y).
